                   oboInOwl:id "UBERON:2002124" ;
                   oboInOwl:inSubset core:human_subset ,
                                     core:mouse_subset ;
                   rdfs:comment """Nuptial tubercles may be keratinized or nonkeratinized. Also may function in territorial defense or stimulation of females in breeding.

Definition reference: Wiley, M. L. and B. B. Collette. 1970. Breeding tubercles and contact organs in fishes: Their occurrence, structure, and significance. Bull Am Mus Nat Hist 143: 143-216.""" ;
                   rdfs:label "nuptial tubercle" .

